  "composition_summary": "Preserved the volatile tail unchanged (single user request, no justified repair). Drafted one pure-logic class-22 component pc-transfer-01 with name/description/content only, per the supported offline-design sink. The body is executable Python at module scope: it reads raw inputs via inputs.get() so missing/empty window is a valid validation outcome, accepts only exact integers in -3..6 inclusive (rejecting bool/float/strings), and assigns result on every branch without raising or coercing. result is {accepted:boolean, window:original if accepted else null}. No imports, I/O, host calls or LLM step. This is an unapproved draft; typed-input transport and Monty runner support remain prerequisites, and no observed tests, submission or activation occurred. No class-21/1-3/13 proposals were made because the sink does not support those constructors here.",
